# 第二部分：English Version

## 1. Purpose of This Agreement

This agreement is intended to protect the intellectual property rights of the authors and contributors of the Kancolle_to_CHS project and to establish clear rules governing the use of project materials.

It is a protective copyright agreement and is not intended to prohibit all forms of legitimate use or cooperation.

Individuals, organizations, or other parties wishing to use, modify, integrate, distribute, or otherwise cooperate using the Materials may contact the project author to request authorization.

Use is permitted only within the scope of authorization expressly granted in writing by the relevant copyright holder.

## 2. Copyright Ownership

The project includes, but is not limited to:

- Source code and related scripts.
- Chinese translations, game text databases, and translation dictionaries.
- Localized game interface assets, modified images, and related artwork.
- Configuration files, data files, and other project resources.
- Documentation and other original project content.

All original materials in which the project authors or contributors hold copyright or other applicable intellectual property rights remain the property of their respective rights holders.

Unless explicitly stated otherwise, no individual or organization may assume that the Materials are freely available for use, modification, or redistribution.

Public availability of this repository on GitHub does not constitute an automatic grant of permission or license.

## 3. Restrictions on Use

Without prior written authorization from the relevant copyright holder, no individual or organization may:

1. Copy, reproduce, extract, or republish any part of the Materials.
2. Modify, translate, adapt, or create derivative works based on the Materials for public distribution.
3. Incorporate the translation files, images, data files, or other project assets into third-party games, software, or projects.
4. Use the Materials in private servers, unofficial game servers, emulated servers, or other unauthorized game services.
5. Use the Materials for commercial operations, paid services, commercial products, or other profit-making activities.
6. Sell, rent, sublicense, or otherwise commercially exploit the Materials.
7. Remove, alter, or conceal original copyright notices, author attributions, or ownership information.
8. Circumvent the authorization requirements of this agreement through renaming files, changing file formats, restructuring directories, or other technical means.

These restrictions apply only to materials over which the relevant copyright holders possess enforceable rights. Nothing in this agreement is intended to restrict fair use or other statutory exceptions permitted by applicable law.

## 4. Authorization Requests

Legitimate requests for use and cooperation are welcome.

Any individual or organization wishing to use any part of the Materials, including for personal projects, further development, game localization, server integration, commercial cooperation, or other purposes, must obtain prior written authorization from the project author.

Requests should include:

- The name of the applicant or organization.
- The specific Materials intended to be used.
- The intended purpose and scope of use.
- Whether modification, integration, or redistribution is involved.
- Whether commercial activities or other profit-making activities are involved.
- The expected duration of use and distribution channels.

The relevant copyright holders reserve the right to approve or reject authorization requests and to determine the scope, duration, and conditions of any authorization.

An authorization request, correspondence, or unapproved application shall not be interpreted as permission to use the Materials.

## 5. Contributors and Third-Party Materials

This project may contain code, translations, images, or other materials contributed by third parties.

Unless otherwise agreed, contributors retain the rights they are legally entitled to hold.

No contributor may grant authorization for third-party materials over which they do not possess the necessary rights.

For jointly created works or materials involving third-party rights, all necessary permissions must be obtained from the relevant rights holders.

## 6. Third-Party Intellectual Property

This project may reference or contain materials associated with *Kantai Collection*, including original game content, character names, artwork, game text, and other third-party assets.

All such original materials and related intellectual property rights remain the property of their respective rights holders.

The project authors do not claim ownership of such third-party original materials, nor does this agreement grant any permission to use third-party intellectual property.

Users are responsible for obtaining all necessary permissions from the relevant third-party rights holders.

## 7. Unauthorized Use and Enforcement

In the event of unauthorized use, reproduction, distribution, or commercial exploitation of copyright-protected Materials, the relevant copyright holders reserve the right to take appropriate action under applicable law.

To the extent permitted by applicable law, such actions may include:

- Demanding the cessation of unauthorized use and distribution.
- Requesting the removal or takedown of unauthorized content.
- Submitting copyright infringement complaints to GitHub, online platforms, and service providers.
- Seeking appropriate legal remedies and compensation for damages.
- Pursuing other lawful measures to protect their rights.

## 8. Termination of Authorization

Any authorization granted under a separate written agreement shall be governed by the terms of that agreement.

In the event of a breach of the applicable authorization conditions, the copyright holder may take measures, including termination of authorization, in accordance with the relevant agreement and applicable law.

Any obligations and legal consequences following termination shall be governed by applicable law and the relevant authorization agreement.

## 9. Reservation of Rights

All rights not expressly granted through a separate written authorization are reserved by the relevant copyright holders.

No right to use, modify, distribute, or otherwise exploit the Materials shall be implied unless expressly granted.

Nothing in this agreement shall restrict fair use or other statutory rights permitted by applicable law.

## 10. Contact and Authorization Requests

For licensing inquiries, authorization requests, or cooperation proposals, please contact the project author through the official GitHub repository.

Repository:

https://github.com/asaico/Kancolle_to_CHS

